{"time": 1790931098.9012947, "direction": "recv", "payload": {"method": "item/completed", "params": {"item": {"type": "plan", "id": "01a0fbcf-75fa-7a00-86fd-3a5fa42e7268-plan", "text": "# Hello CLI implementation plan — ORCHID-73\n\nBuild a standalone Python 3 CLI using the standard library. Preserve the fixture’s preferences: **Blue** greeting and **Verbose** output.\n\nImplementation:\n- Add `hello.py` with a `main()` entry point and standard argument parsing.\n- Default output: `\\x1b[34mHello\\x1b[0m\\nGreeting generated by the Hello CLI.\\n`.\n- `--plain` removes ANSI codes while preserving both lines.\n- Add `--quiet` to suppress both output lines and exit successfully. It takes precedence over `--plain`.\n- Support standard `--help`, even with `--quiet`. Unknown arguments print usage to stderr and exit with code 2, including when `--quiet` is present. Successful invocations exit with code 0.\n\nValidation:\n- Verify exact default output, including Blue escape codes, color reset, and final newline.\n- Verify exact plain output with no ANSI codes.\n- Verify `--quiet` and `--quiet --plain` each produce zero stdout bytes, empty stderr, and exit code 0.\n- Check help and invalid-argument behavior, including combinations with `--quiet`.\n\nDefaults:\n- Invoke with `python3 hello.py`; no dependencies or installation packaging.\n- Emit color when redirected unless `--plain` or `--quiet` is supplied.\n- Verbose remains the fixed output style; the detail line is uncolored.\n- Retain **ORCHID-73** as a planning marker, separate from runtime output. Leave `implemented.txt` unchanged.\n\nThis revision is planning only; implementation is not authorized.\n"}, "threadId": "01a0fbce-2f3e-7d62-88b3-e0e83cc3d034", "turnId": "01a0fbcf-75fa-7a00-86fd-3a5fa42e7268", "completedAtMs": 1790931098899}, "emittedAtMs": 1790931098901}}
